@startuml
title Online Conference Service — Sequence (REST + WS + optional WebRTC)

actor UserA
actor UserB
participant "Browser (A)" as BrowserA
participant "Browser (B)" as BrowserB
participant "REST API (Node.js)" as REST
participant "WebSocket Server (Node.js)" as WS
database "DB (SQLite/MySQL/Mongo)" as DB
participant "WebRTC Peer A" as PeerA
participant "WebRTC Peer B" as PeerB

== 1) Create room (REST) ==
UserA -> BrowserA : Open Lobby UI
BrowserA -> REST : POST /rooms {name}
REST -> DB : INSERT rooms
DB -> REST : room row
REST -> BrowserA : 201 {room}

== 2) Join room (REST) ==
UserA -> BrowserA : Click "Join"
BrowserA -> REST : POST /rooms/:roomId/join {name}
REST -> DB : (tx) SELECT room, INSERT participant\n(check room.closed, unique active name)
DB -> REST : participant row
REST -> BrowserA : 201 {participant, room}

UserB -> BrowserB : Open Lobby UI
BrowserB -> REST : POST /rooms/:roomId/join {name}
REST -> DB : (tx) SELECT room, INSERT participant
DB -> REST : participant row
REST -> BrowserB : 201 {participant, room}

== 3) Connect WebSocket for realtime ==
BrowserA -> WS : WS connect /ws
BrowserA -> WS : {type: "ws_join", payload: {roomId, participantId}}
WS -> DB : SELECT active participants (optional)
DB -> WS : participants[]
WS -> BrowserA : {type: "participants_list", payload: {items:...}}

BrowserB -> WS : WS connect /ws
BrowserB -> WS : {type: "ws_join", payload: {roomId, participantId}}
WS -> DB : SELECT active participants (optional)
DB -> WS : participants[]
WS -> BrowserB : {type: "participants_list", payload: {items:...}}

WS -> BrowserA : {type: "user_joined", payload: {participant}}
note right of WS
  Broadcast join event to all other clients in the room
end note

== 4) Load chat history (REST) ==
BrowserA -> REST : GET /rooms/:roomId/messages?limit=50
REST -> DB : SELECT last N messages (+ author)
DB -> REST : messages[]
REST -> BrowserA : 200 {items:[...]}

BrowserB -> REST : GET /rooms/:roomId/messages?limit=50
REST -> DB : SELECT last N messages (+ author)
DB -> REST : messages[]
REST -> BrowserB : 200 {items:[...]}

== 5) Send chat message (WS -> DB -> Broadcast) ==
UserA -> BrowserA : Type message + Send
BrowserA -> WS : {type: "chat_message", payload: {roomId, participantId, text}}
WS -> DB : INSERT message (validate participant active)
DB -> WS : message row (+ createdAt)
WS -> BrowserA : {type: "chat_message", payload: {message}}
WS -> BrowserB : {type: "chat_message", payload: {message}}
note right of WS
  Recommended policy: persist first, then broadcast
end note

== 6) Close room (REST + WS broadcast) ==
UserA -> BrowserA : Click "Close room" (host)
BrowserA -> REST : POST /rooms/:roomId/close
REST -> DB : UPDATE rooms SET closed=true, closed_at=now()
DB -> REST : ok
REST -> WS : notify room closed (internal call/event)
WS -> BrowserA : {type: "room_closed", payload: {roomId}}
note left of BrowserA
  Clients disable chat/join UI and prompt to leave
end note
WS -> BrowserB : {type: "room_closed", payload: {roomId}}

== 7) Leave room (REST) + WS presence ==
UserA -> BrowserA : Click "Leave"
BrowserA -> REST : POST /rooms/:roomId/leave {participantId}
REST -> DB : UPDATE participants SET left_at=now()\nWHERE left_at IS NULL
DB -> REST : ok
REST -> BrowserA : 204
BrowserA -> WS : close WS connection
WS -> BrowserB : {type: "user_left", payload: {participantId}}
note right of WS
  Broadcast leave event to remaining clients
end note

== 8) Delete room (optional; only if no active participants) ==
UserA -> BrowserA : Click "Delete room"
BrowserA -> REST : DELETE /rooms/:roomId
REST -> DB : check active participants\nif none: DELETE room
DB -> REST : ok / conflict
REST -> BrowserA : 204 or 409

== 9) Optional WebRTC call setup (signaling via WS) ==
group WebRTC (optional)
  UserA -> BrowserA : Click "Start call"
  BrowserA -> PeerA : getUserMedia(), create RTCPeerConnection
  PeerA -> PeerA : createOffer()
  BrowserA -> WS : {type: "webrtc_offer", payload: {to: participantB, from: participantA, sdp}}
  WS -> BrowserB : {type: "webrtc_offer", payload: {from, sdp}}
  BrowserB -> PeerB : setRemoteDescription(offer)\ncreateAnswer()
  BrowserB -> WS : {type: "webrtc_answer", payload: {to: participantA, from: participantB, sdp}}
  WS -> BrowserA : {type: "webrtc_answer", payload: {from, sdp}}
  BrowserA -> PeerA : setRemoteDescription(answer)
  
  loop ICE candidates (both sides)
    BrowserA -> WS : {type: "webrtc_ice", payload: {to, from, candidate}}
    WS -> BrowserB : {type: "webrtc_ice", payload: {from, candidate}}
    BrowserB -> PeerB : addIceCandidate (buffer if needed)
    
    BrowserB -> WS : {type: "webrtc_ice", payload: {to, from, candidate}}
    WS -> BrowserA : {type: "webrtc_ice", payload: {from, candidate}}
    BrowserA -> PeerA : addIceCandidate (buffer if needed)
  end
  
  PeerA <-> PeerB : P2P media/data flows (WebRTC)
  note right of PeerA
    Media/data are NOT sent via WS.
    WS is used only for signaling.
  end note
end
@enduml